      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} && R_{1}\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $2$nd and $4$th columns.",
