      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} && R_{1}\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns.",
      ":question/id": "0ba6526a-fef7-518b-979b-7aeb66d1d2a7",
