    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} && R_{2}\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns.",
