    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} && R_{1}\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns.",
